      "title": "Input Text (Prompt)",
      "properties": {
        "cnr_id": "comfy-core",
        "ver": "0.29.0",
        "Node name for S&R": "PrimitiveStringMultiline"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "Create a 10-second, 16:9 Axon Signal short from the supplied references.\n\nUse <Picture 1> only for the original engineer's identity, graphite utility\nsuit, amber shoulder line, and signal prism. If <Video 1> is present, use it\nonly for body motion and camera timing, not appearance. If <Audio 1> is present,\nuse it only for voice texture and cadence; do not copy words.\n\n[0–3s] Medium close-up in a dark brutalist observatory. The engineer studies the\nblack prism while a restrained amber pulse moves through it. Slow handheld\nbreathing, stable face and hands.\n\n[3–7s] Match the movement rhythm from <Video 1> when available: the engineer\nturns and walks toward a circular antenna. A single amber signal follows along\nthe floor. Maintain spatial continuity and the reference identity.\n\n[7–10s] The engineer says, in a newly generated line, “Signal locked.” Match the\ncadence of <Audio 1> only when present. The antenna sends one amber ring into the\ncloud layer. End on the engineer in clear three-quarter profile.\n\nAudio: native stereo wind, electrical hum, relay clicks, original restrained\nvoice, and one low analog pulse. No copyrighted characters, brands, copied\ndialogue, extra people, text overlays, logos, watermarks, identity drift,\nwardrobe changes, random camera spins, or particle explosions."
      ],
      "color": "#322",
      "bgcolor": "#533"
    },
